{"id":"S9002","name":"Diskpart","description":"Diskpart is a Windows command-line utility that is used to manage the computer’s drives, which includes disks, partitions, volumes and virtual hard disks. Adversaries may abuse Diskpart to perform discovery and destructive actions on a system’s storage. For example, adversaries have been observed using Diskpart to conduct Discovery techniques to enumerate disks and volumes to gather information about the host environment, and to execute commands such as `clean all` to remove partition information and overwrite data across disks, resulting in data destruction.","kind":"attack_tool","upstream_type":"tool","stix_id":"tool--080f872e-f1a3-4d42-bb00-9eb55949f6a9","source_modified":"2026-04-23T02:11:05.517Z","aliases":["Diskpart"],"platforms":["Windows"],"source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/software/S9002","source_domains":["enterprise"],"classification_note":"Included because the active pinned ATT&CK object has type tool. This is an upstream classification, not an assurance of benignness or a recommendation to run it.","page":"tools/S9002/","reviewed_on":"2026-09-27","guides":[],"guide_currentness":"Historical guides retain publication dates. Commands and product availability have not been revalidated.","techniques":[{"key":"enterprise/T1059.003","id":"T1059.003","name":"Windows Command Shell","domain":"enterprise","page":"techniques/enterprise/T1059.003/","environments":["cloud-hosted-endpoint","onprem"],"platforms":["Windows"],"bases":["attack_uses"],"evidence":[{"basis":"attack_uses","relationship_id":"relationship--cef1859a-f4d6-42ca-9fa8-eb77b7ae6e7b","description":"Diskpart can execute a disk partition script file, which attempts to mount a virtual hard disk. Diskpart can also assign and mount virtual disks.","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/software/S9002","source_commit":"6cda5ad8462c79e14fbb872f4e09059b18e0cfc4","citations":[{"title":"Halcyon RISE Team. (2024, December 12). Cloak Ransomware Variant Exhibits Advanced Persistence, Evasion and VHD Extraction Capabilities. Retrieved December 23, 2025.","url":"https://www.halcyon.ai/blog/cloak-ransomware-variant-exhibits-advanced-persistence-evasion-and-vhd-extraction-capabilities"}]}],"telemetry_references":[{"id":"DC0016","name":"Module Load","tag":"Module Load","page":"telemetry/DC0016/","kind":"attack_component"},{"id":"DC0032","name":"Process Creation","tag":"Process Creation","page":"telemetry/DC0032/","kind":"attack_component"},{"id":"DC0029","name":"Script Execution","tag":"Script Execution","page":"telemetry/DC0029/","kind":"attack_component"}]},{"key":"enterprise/T1082","id":"T1082","name":"System Information Discovery","domain":"enterprise","page":"techniques/enterprise/T1082/","environments":["cloud","cloud-hosted-endpoint","network-infrastructure","onprem","virtualization"],"platforms":["ESXi","IaaS","Linux","macOS","Network Devices","Windows"],"bases":["attack_uses"],"evidence":[{"basis":"attack_uses","relationship_id":"relationship--5619736a-4081-4fc3-93b7-cf70d01cd094","description":"Diskpart can show information about the selected disk, partition, volume, or virtual hard disk (VHD).","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/software/S9002","source_commit":"6cda5ad8462c79e14fbb872f4e09059b18e0cfc4","citations":[{"title":"Microsoft. (2023, February 3). diskpart. Retrieved March 17, 2025.","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows-server/administration/windows-commands/diskpart"}]}],"telemetry_references":[{"id":"DC0064","name":"Command Execution","tag":"Command Execution","page":"telemetry/DC0064/","kind":"attack_component"},{"id":"DC0075","name":"Instance Enumeration","tag":"Instance Enumeration","page":"telemetry/DC0075/","kind":"attack_component"},{"id":"DC0032","name":"Process Creation","tag":"Process Creation","page":"telemetry/DC0032/","kind":"attack_component"},{"id":"DC0063","name":"Windows Registry Key Modification","tag":"Windows Registry Key Modification","page":"telemetry/DC0063/","kind":"atta